Rolling Update of Nginx Deployment to v1.19
This task involved performing a rolling update on an existing Kubernetes deployment (nginx-deployment) to update its container image to nginx:1.19.

Task Overview
Cluster Environment: KodeKloud Engineer jump-host / Kubernetes cluster.

Target Object: Deployment (nginx-deployment).

Objective: Update the deployment container image to nginx:1.19 using a rolling update mechanism and ensure all pods successfully transition and become operational.

Execution Steps
Identify Container Name:
Query the deployment template to find the exact container name defined under the pod specification:

Bash
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[*].name}'
(Result identified: nginx-container)

Execute Rolling Update:
Update the deployment's container image to nginx:1.19:

Bash
kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deployment nginx-container=nginx:1.19
Verify Rollout Status:
Monitor the progress of the rolling update until all pods are running and healthy:

Bash
kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deployment
Verification & Results
Rollout Status: deployment "nginx-deployment" successfully rolled out

